  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03280v2</id>
    <title>Training Optimal Large Diffusion Language Models</title>
    <updated>2025-11-05T08:32:08Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03280v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.03280v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We introduce Quokka, the first systematic scaling law for diffusion language models (DLMs), encompassing both compute-constrained and data-constrained regimes, and studying the key modeling and optimization designs. Quokka is a good friend of Chinchilla and provides wider scopes. We hope the results would bring short-term practical guidance in DLMs training and long-term inspirations for the whole AI community.</summary>
    <category term="cs.LG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
